<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">Investment Through Wholly Owned Subsidiary.&#160; </font>The Master Fund&#8217;s assets may be invested in an Underlying Fund through its wholly-owned and controlled foreign subsidiary, Ironwood Multi-Strategy Fund Ltd. (the <font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">&#8220;Subsidiary&#8221;</font>).</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">The Subsidiary has the same investment objective as the Master Fund and does not receive investment advice separate from the Master Fund.&#160; The Subsidiary&#8217;s sole director is a director of the Master Fund.</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">The Master Fund complies with the provisions of the 1940 Act governing investment policies (Section 8) and capital structure and leverage (Section 18) on an aggregate basis with the Subsidiary.&#160; The Subsidiary complies with all provisions of the 1940 Act governing affiliated transactions and custody (Section 17).&#160; As of the date of this SAI, none of the Master Fund&#8217;s assets are invested through the Subsidiary.</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; TEXT-ALIGN: center">DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold; TEXT-ALIGN: left">Directors</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'">The Board has ultimate responsibility </font><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'">for overseeing</font> the business and operations of the Feeder Fund on behalf of its members.&#160; At least a majority of the Board are and will remain persons who are not &#8220;interested persons,&#8221; as defined in Section 2(a)(19) of the 1940 Act (&#8220;<font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">Independent Directors</font>&#8221;).&#160; Subject to the provisions of the Limited Liability Company Agreements of the Feeder Fund and the Master Fund (each, an &#8220;<font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">LLC Agreement</font>&#8221; and collectively, the &#8220;<font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">LLC Agreements</font>&#8221;) and Delaware law, the Directors will have all powers necessary and convenient to carry out this responsibility.</font></div>

