<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">Additional information about each Director follows (supplementing the information provided in the table above) that describes some of the specific experiences, qualifications, attributes or skills that each Director possesses which the Board believes has prepared them to be effective Directors.</div>

<div>&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">Jonathan Gans </font>is the Chief Executive Officer and President of Ironwood.&#160; He joined the firm in 1996 and is a member of Ironwood&#8217;s Investment &amp; Risk Committee, Leadership Committee, Management Committee, and Valuation Committee.&#160; He also serves as a Director for Ironwood&#8217;s offshore and registered funds.&#160; Jon was previously employed at St. Claire Capital Management, where he was General Counsel and Chief Operating Officer.&#160; His prior professional experience also includes positions at the Securities and Exchange Commission Division of Enforcement and Glenwood Financial Group.&#160; Jon earned a B.A., cum laude, from Williams College, a J.D. from the University of California at Los Angeles School of Law, and is a member of the State Bar of California.&#160; Jon is a chapter member of YPO Golden Gate and a Trustee of the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art (SFMOMA), where he has chaired the Investment Committee and served on the Executive Committee.</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><br>
</div>

<div style="TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">
<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.25; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">Richard W. Meadows </font>serves as an Independent Director for each of Ironwood&#8217;s registered funds, Ironwood Institutional Multi-Strategy Fund LLC and Ironwood Multi-Strategy Fund LLC.&#160; In 2010, Rick retired from a near-thirty year career in the alternative investment industry.&#160; After acting as a hedge fund manager and then managing a fund of hedge funds similar in structure to some of the private Ironwood funds in the 1980&#8217;s, he&#160;co-founded and served as president of Price Meadows Incorporated, a hedge fund administration company that came to be recognized by Institutional Investor&#8217;s Alpha Awards as being among the five best such firms in the nation.&#160; As an administration firm, PMI was involved in back office operations, performance calculation and reporting plus audit support for hundreds of hedge funds and funds of funds.&#160; Rick specialized in team management, document review and expansion of services.&#160; In 2008, PMI was acquired by ALPS Fund Services Inc.&#160; Rick&#160;served as Executive Vice President of the acquiring firm until his retirement in 2010.&#160; He earned a B.S. degree in Business from the University of Idaho, and holds a Masters Degree in Business Administration from Washington State University. In addition to the Funds, he advises and serves on the boards of several private companies.</div>

<div style="LINE-HEIGHT: 1.25">&#160;</div>

<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.25; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt"><font style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; FONT-WEIGHT: bold">M. Kelley Price</font> serves as an Independent Director for each of Ironwood&#8217;s registered funds, Ironwood Institutional Multi-Strategy Fund LLC and Ironwood Multi-Strategy Fund LLC and serves as chair of the audit committee.&#160; In 2010, Kelley retired from a near-thirty year career in the alternative investment industry.&#160; After acting as a hedge fund manager and then managing a fund of hedge funds similar in structure to some of the private Ironwood funds in the 1980&#8217;s, he co-founded Price Meadows Incorporated, a hedge fund administration company that came to be recognized by Institutional Investor&#8217;s Alpha Awards as being among the five best such firms in the nation.&#160; As an administration firm, PMI was involved in back office operations, performance calculation and reporting plus audit support for hundreds of hedge funds and funds of funds.&#160; Kelley specialized in automating the accounting processes and providing resources for clients.&#160; In 2008, PMI was acquired by ALPS Fund Services Inc.&#160; Kelley served as Executive Vice President of the acquiring firm until his retirement in 2010.&#160; He is a 1972 graduate of Stanford University.&#160; In addition to the Funds, he advises or serves on the boards of several private companies.</div>
</div>

