<div style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: 'Times New Roman'; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; TEXT-INDENT: 36pt">The Distribution Agreement may be terminated, without the payment of any penalty:&#160; (i) through a failure to renew the Distribution Agreement at the end of a term, or (ii) upon mutual consent of the Fund and the Distributor.&#160; Further, the Distribution Agreement may be terminated upon no less than 60 days&#8217; written notice, by either the Fund through a vote of a majority of the members of the Board who are not interested persons, as that term is defined in the 1940 Act, and have no direct or indirect financial interest in the operation of the Distribution Agreement or by a vote of a majority of the outstanding Units of the Fund, in accordance with, and as defined in, Section 15 of the 1940 Act, or by the Distributor.</div>

